      "value": "@{5aa9533aa739da06e6018df6|full_name}: It only takes a few bad apples to ruin a good thing for everyone. As a good example, ask any small community Discord server why they aren't allowing all users to use the `@everyone` ping, it takes only one person abusing once or twice before the server owners just remove the permission from everyone on the server.\n\nAnd besides, the world creator moderation powers are redundant now that they can just use a Group Public instance instead. That way players joining the instance will also know that the instance is moderated, since most VRChat users don't even know that world creator moderation powers exist.\n\nAnyway, this is better discussed in my above linked feature request.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
