      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{610d538d5303a82960a415b4|full_name}: Sorry I haven't kept up with this. So this didn't happen to me, but to a friend, and it was a Group Public I do believe, she joined to see the group, and talk to people about her world, when the instance owner thinking they were funny, kicked her from the instance of the world. If it was a private instance, Id say the ability for the instance owner to be able to kick people is fine, but I'm pretty sure it was a group public, and being able to kick the owner from a group public, even though it is a group, just seems very wrong, especially if in a scenario, people in said group public were breaking rules of the world, shouldnt the World Owner still have the ability to enforce rules on any public world? Be it Group or not Group?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
